# .pii-allow — values pii.scan is allowed to ignore
#
# the allowlist is by VALUE, never by file. a file-scoped mute blinds a
# whole file forever — even against the next value someone pastes into
# it. a value-scoped one costs exactly one deliberate, reviewable line
# per number, which is the point: each line here is a decision a human
# made and a reviewer can check.
#
# an entry matches on its digits, so one line covers both the formatted
# and the bare form (666-12-3456 also mutes 666123456).
#
# every entry needs a comment that states WHY it is safe. an entry with
# no reason reads exactly like a leak someone silenced.

# SSA has never issued a 666 prefix, so this is structurally valid and
# permanently synthetic. used as the SSN fixture in the pdf.redact and
# pii.scan tests.
666-12-3456

# IRS example EIN, published in Pub 1635 as a documentation placeholder.
00-0000000

# all-zero and sequential runs that appear in form templates and blank
# field examples; never a real identifier. 123-45-6789 also covers the
# bare 123456789 used as a synthetic EIN in the pdf.redact tests.
000-00-0000
123-45-6789

# the multi-SSN fixture in the pdf.redact tests. each is a run of
# repeated-digit groups in ascending order — a shape no real SSN takes.
111-22-3333
444-55-6666

# the synthetic address fixture in the pii.scan street-detector test.
# an entry must match the span the detector reports, which ends at the
# unit word — so the house number after "Apt" is not part of it.
500 Fake Street Apt

# ── the v2020_05_17.sandpine example packet ─────────────────────────────
#
# every value below was WRITTEN BY `doc.pseudonymize` from a map, and the
# set verifies clean (`--verify`, survivors: 0). these entries mute the
# SHAPES the detectors correctly matched on invented values.
#
# ⚠️ do not extend this block by hand. if a new hit appears in that
#    directory, the correct move is a new pair in the map and a re-run —
#    never a new line here.

# synthetic EIN on the CP 575 notice.
99-0001234

# synthetic Delaware authentication number on the certified charter copy.
# 9 digits, so both the ssn and ein detectors claim it.
201122334

# synthetic residence, in the two casings the source documents print.
2200 North Cascade Ave Apt
2200 N CASCADE AVE APT

# synthetic third-party-designee office on the SS-4.
4400 Meridian Way, Suite

# the registered-agent office in Middletown DE. a commercial address
# printed on every Delaware charter that agent files — public by design,
# and NOT the entity's own address. kept because the packet is unreadable
# without it.
651 N Broad St, Suite

# the IRS public phone lines printed on every CP 575 notice: business
# assistance, forms, and TTY/TDD. published by the IRS; not PII.
800-829-4933
800-829-3676
800-829-4059

# ── published agency contact lines ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠️ these are here to keep the scanner CREDIBLE, not to be lenient. a
#    report that flags a government agency's own published phone number
#    on 20+ briefs trains its readers to skim past the report — and a
#    gate nobody reads protects nobody. an over-eager detector is not
#    the safe direction to err.
#
# ⛔ the test is PUBLISHED BY THE ORGANIZATION, not merely "a business
#    number". a number that reaches one named individual is PII even at
#    a government office, and does NOT belong here — see the extension
#    numbers deliberately left out.

# Delaware Division of Corporations, Franchise Tax queue. printed on
# corp.delaware.gov/taxfaq and quoted verbatim in the statutes briefs.
302-739-3073

# Delaware Division of Corporations, the address paper filings go to.
# printed on corp.delaware.gov and quoted in the revival/amendment
# stones. an agency's own counter, not anyone's residence.
401 Federal Street

# Florida notary lines, printed in the Governor's own Notary Reference
# Manual, which this repo carries VERBATIM as an embedded source (see
# briefs/jurats/refs/…effectiveAt=2019-12-17…). the manual must not be
# edited — a citation you altered is not a citation — so an allowlist
# entry is the only correct move here.
#   717-9310 = Exec Office of the Governor, Notary Section
#   245-6975 / 245-6945 = Dept of State, Notary Commissions
#   488-2952 = the agency line printed at p. 220
850-717-9310
850-245-6975
850-245-6945
850-488-2952

# USPTO's published assistance line, printed at the foot of every office
# action. appears in the patent.priors transcription fixtures as OCR'd
# from the form itself.
800-770-3199

# the boilerplate service lines the USPTO prints on EVERY filing receipt
# and Notice of Publication. they reach a division or a unit, never a
# named individual, and they are the numbers the form itself tells the
# applicant to call. OCR'd verbatim into the patent.priors fixtures.
#   786-9199 = USPTO Contact Center
#   272-3150 / 972-6382 = Public Records Division (direct + toll-free)
#   273-3250 = Public Records Division facsimile
#   217-9197 = Patent Electronic Business Center
#   272-4000 / 272-4200 / 786-0101 = Office of Data Management,
#                                    Application Assistance Unit
800-786-9199
571-272-3150
800-972-6382
571-273-3250
866-217-9197
571-272-4000
571-272-4200
888-786-0101

# two US Government hotlines printed on the same filing-receipt page.
# both are public-facing programs, not USPTO desks.
#   866-999-4258 = 1-866-999-HALT, the interagency IP enforcement line
#   202-482-6800 = SelectUSA, Dept of Commerce
866-999-4258
202-482-6800

# American Express Customer Care, printed on every Amex statement. it is
# in the statement.parse fixture because the parser has to skip past the
# header block, and a header with the phone line removed would not
# exercise that. the rest of that fixture is synthetic.
800-521-6121

# the NANP reserved block for fiction: 555-0100 through 555-0199 can
# never be assigned to a live subscriber. used for the synthetic
# attorney in the patent.priors cached-patent fixture.
#
# 👉 reach for this block first when a fixture needs a phone-shaped
#    value. a made-up number is somebody's real line.
202-555-0100

